From: xiaobao <18916331286@189.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] mesa: enable panfrost gallium driver on arm/aarch64

Branch: master    Version: 25.0.7    Release: 3 -> 4

openEuler's gallium driver list has no panfrost, so on aarch64 boards with a
Mali GPU (RK3576 / Mali-G52 MC3) mesa-dri-drivers ships only swrast and
kms_swrast plus the kmsro dummy display drivers, and GLX/EGL/GBM fall back to
software rendering. panfrost does not require LLVM, so enabling it costs only
one extra driver object. This is the same switch Fedora already carries
(with_panfrost plus the panfrost token in its gallium driver list).

Generated with signature: xiaobao <18916331286@189.cn>  issue #<ISSUE_NUMBER>
NOTE: rebase the hunks onto the PR base commit if mesa.spec moved since.

--- a/mesa.spec
+++ b/mesa.spec
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@
 %define with_vc4       1
 %define with_v3d       1
 %define with_kmsro     1
+%define with_panfrost  1
 %endif
 
 %ifarch riscv64
@@ -65,7 +66,7 @@
 Name:           mesa
 Summary:        Mesa graphics libraries
 Version:        25.0.7
-Release:        3
+Release:        4
 
 License:        MIT
 URL:            https://www.mesa3d.org
@@ -333,7 +334,7 @@
   -Dplatforms=x11,wayland \
   -Dosmesa=true \
 %if 0%{?with_hardware}
-  -Dgallium-drivers=softpipe,llvmpipe%{?with_iris:,iris},virgl,nouveau%{?with_vmware:,svga},radeonsi,r300,r600%{?with_freedreno:,freedreno}%{?with_etnaviv:,etnaviv}%{?with_tegra:,tegra}%{?with_vc4:,vc4}%{?with_v3d:,v3d}%{?with_crocus:,crocus}%{?with_vulkan_hw:,zink} \
+  -Dgallium-drivers=softpipe,llvmpipe%{?with_iris:,iris},virgl,nouveau%{?with_vmware:,svga},radeonsi,r300,r600%{?with_freedreno:,freedreno}%{?with_etnaviv:,etnaviv}%{?with_tegra:,tegra}%{?with_vc4:,vc4}%{?with_v3d:,v3d}%{?with_panfrost:,panfrost}%{?with_crocus:,crocus}%{?with_vulkan_hw:,zink} \
 %else
   -Dgallium-drivers=softpipe,llvmpipe,virgl \
 %endif
@@ -490,6 +491,9 @@
 %endif
 %if 0%{?with_v3d}
 %{_libdir}/dri/v3d_dri.so
+%endif
+%if 0%{?with_panfrost}
+%{_libdir}/dri/panfrost_dri.so
 %endif
 %if 0%{?with_kmsro}
 %{_libdir}/dri/armada-drm_dri.so
@@ -593,6 +597,12 @@
 %endif
 
 %changelog
+* Tue Nov 24 2026 xiaobao <18916331286@189.cn> - 25.0.7-4
+- enable panfrost gallium driver on arm/aarch64, so boards with a Mali GPU
+  (e.g. RK3576 / Mali-G52 MC3) get hardware GL/EGL/GBM from
+  mesa-dri-drivers instead of silently falling back to software rendering.
+  See issue #<ISSUE_NUMBER>.
+
 * Wed Jul 08 2026 Wenlong Zhang <zhangwenlong@loongson.cn> - 25.0.7-3
 - zink_dri.so is unpackaged on loongarch64
 
